## std/sourcemap.pengu — byte offsets ↔ `(line, column)` for source text.
##
## A `SourceMap` indexes the line starts of one immutable source string and
## answers the two questions every tool that reports positions asks: *what
## `(line, column)` is this byte offset?* and *what byte offset is this
## `(line, column)`?* Construction is O(n), `position_at` is O(log n) and
## `offset_of` is O(1).
##
## ## Conventions
## - Lines and columns are **1-indexed**, like every editor and compiler
##   diagnostic.
## - A column is a **byte** offset within the line, not a codepoint index.
##   `"ñ"` is one line of two bytes, so column 2 is its second byte. This is the
##   right choice for a compiler or a diff tool: it makes `offset = start + col
##   - 1` exact, including for invalid UTF-8, and it never makes a span point at
##   half a character because of a width table.
## - `\n` starts a new line. In a `\r\n` pair the `\r` is part of the line's
##   bytes (so offsets stay exact) but is **not** included in `line_text`.
## - A source string may be empty; it still has one (empty) line.
##
## ## Ownership
## `from_source` **copies** the source into the map. The map is independent of
## the string it was built from; that string may be released immediately.
## `line_text` and `substring` return **owned** strings that the caller must
## `banish`. `source` returns the map's own copy **borrowed**: do not banish it.
## `banish sourcemap` releases both the source copy and the line-start list.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## import std.sourcemap
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var map as SourceMap is calling SourceMap.from_source with "hola\nmundo\n"
##     defer banish map
##     var p as Position is calling map.position_at with 6
##     calling spark.println with "line {p.line}, col {p.col}"   # line 2, col 1
##     var off as int is calling map.offset_of with 2, 3
##     calling spark.println with "{off}"                        # 8
##     var line as string is calling map.line_text with 2
##     defer banish line
##     calling spark.println with line                          # mundo
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `from_source` | O(n) bytes and O(number of lines) |
## | `position_at` | O(log lines) |
## | `offset_of`, `line_count`, `source_len` | O(1) |
## | `line_text`, `line_span`, `is_valid_position` | O(line length) |
## | `span_at`, `is_valid_offset`, `clamp_offset` | O(log lines) / O(1) |

import std.spark

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## SourceMap module version.
const SOURCEMAP_VERSION as string is "2.11.0"

## The line terminator recognised by `from_source`.
const SOURCEMAP_NEWLINE as int is 10

## The carriage-return byte stripped from `line_text` in CRLF files.
const SOURCEMAP_CARRIAGE_RETURN as int is 13

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Value types
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## A 1-indexed source position.
##
## ## Memoria
## Value type: no heap fields, nothing to release.
rune Position derive Par:
    line as int
    col as int

## A half-open source range from `start` to `end`.
##
## The end position is exclusive, matching how spans are rendered (`start..end`)
## and how a caret is placed under the first byte of a token.
##
## ## Memoria
## Value type: no heap fields, nothing to release.
rune Span derive Par:
    start as Position
    end as Position

## An immutable source string plus the byte offset where every line starts.
##
## `_line_starts[0]` is always `0`; `_line_starts[i]` is the offset of the first
## byte of line `i + 1`. Line `i + 1` ends at `_line_starts[i + 1] - 1` (the
## `\n`) or at the end of the source for the last line.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns `_source` (a private copy) and `_line_starts`. `banish map` releases
## both through `derive Nexus`.
rune SourceMap derive Nexus:
    _source as string
    _line_starts as list of int

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private C bridges
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Returns a fresh owned copy of `s`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `from_source` must own its source independently of the caller's string.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one buffer; the caller releases it with `banish` (the map does it
## through `Nexus`).
antiquus _sourcemap_copy with s as string into string:
    r"""
return pengu_string_copy(s);
"""

## Returns an owned copy of the byte range `[start, end)` of `s`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `line_text` slices a line and `SourceMap` must return an owned string even
## when the range is empty. The runtime substring helper already does exactly
## this; the wrapper keeps the ownership contract in one place.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one owned buffer; the caller releases it with `banish`.
antiquus _sourcemap_substring with s as string, start as int, end as int into string:
    r"""
return pengu_string_substring(s, start, end);
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Construction
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting SourceMap:
    ## Builds a map for `src`, copying the string and indexing every line start.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `src`: the source text. Borrowed; the map takes its own copy.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A ready-to-query `SourceMap`, even for an empty source (which has one
    ## empty line).
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Allocates one copy of `src` and a `list of int` with one entry per line.
    ## Release the map with `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var map as SourceMap is calling SourceMap.from_source with "a\nb\n"
    ## defer banish map
    ## ```
    weave ritual from_source with src as string into SourceMap:
        var owned_source as string is calling _sourcemap_copy with src
        var starts as list of int is list of int
        calling starts.push with 0
        var n as int is src length
        var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of src
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            if ((raw at i) to int) == SOURCEMAP_NEWLINE:
                calling starts.push with (i + 1)
            set i is i + 1
        return with _source is owned_source, _line_starts is starts

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Queries
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Returns the map's source copy, borrowed.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## The exact bytes passed to `from_source`. **Do not banish it**; the map
    ## owns it and releases it when the map is banished.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation, no ownership transfer.
    weave source into string:
        return self->_source

    ## Returns the number of lines (at least one, even for empty input).
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `_line_starts.len`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation.
    weave line_count into int:
        return self->_line_starts.len

    ## Returns the length of the source in bytes.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A non-negative `int`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation.
    weave source_len into int:
        var sv as string is self->_source
        return sv length

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Position ↔ offset
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Maps a byte offset to its 1-indexed `(line, column)`.
    ##
    ## Offsets outside `[0, source_len]` are **clamped** (negative to `0`,
    ## too-large to `source_len`), so a diagnostic built from a recovered token
    ## never panics. `position_at(source_len)` is the position just after the
    ## last byte (line `line_count`, column `line_len + 1` for a source that
    ## does not end in a newline; line `line_count`, column 1 when it does).
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `offset`: a byte offset; clamped as described.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A `Position` with `line >= 1` and `col >= 1`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(log lines), no allocation.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var p as Position is calling map.position_at with 0
    ## # p.line == 1, p.col == 1
    ## ```
    weave position_at with offset as int into Position:
        var off as int is offset
        var n as int is (calling self.source_len)
        if off < 0:
            set off is 0
        if off > n:
            set off is n
        var lo as int is 0
        var hi as int is self->_line_starts.len - 1
        while lo < hi:
            var mid as int is (lo + hi + 1) / 2
            if (self->_line_starts at mid) <= off:
                set lo is mid
            else:
                set hi is mid - 1
        var start as int is self->_line_starts at lo
        return with line is (lo + 1), col is (off - start + 1)

    ## Maps a 1-indexed `(line, column)` to its byte offset.
    ##
    ## Panics when `line` is outside `[1, line_count]`, when `col < 1`, or when
    ## the column falls past the end of that line. A column one past the last
    ## byte of a line is valid: for a line ending in `\n` it addresses the
    ## newline byte, and for the last line it addresses `source_len`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `line`: 1-indexed line number.
    ## - `col`: 1-indexed byte column.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A byte offset in `[0, source_len]`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation. Panics are fatal (`pengu_panic`).
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var off as int is calling map.offset_of with 1, 1
    ## # off == 0
    ## ```
    weave offset_of with line as int, col as int into int:
        if line < 1 or line > self->_line_starts.len:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.offset_of: line out of range"
        if col < 1:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.offset_of: column must be >= 1"
        var start as int is self->_line_starts at (line - 1)
        var off as int is start + col - 1
        if line < self->_line_starts.len:
            var next_start as int is self->_line_starts at line
            if off >= next_start:
                calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.offset_of: column past end of line"
        else:
            if off > (calling self.source_len):
                calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.offset_of: column past end of source"
        return off

    ## Returns the text of `line` (1-indexed) as an owned string.
    ##
    ## The trailing `\n` is excluded; a trailing `\r` from a CRLF pair is also
    ## excluded. Offsets still count the `\r` and the `\n`, so column arithmetic
    ## on the source stays exact.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `line`: 1-indexed line number.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A new **owned** string. Release it with `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Allocates one buffer of the line length. Panics when `line` is out of
    ## range.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var text as string is calling map.line_text with 1
    ## defer banish text
    ## ```
    weave line_text with line as int into string:
        if line < 1 or line > self->_line_starts.len:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.line_text: line out of range"
        var start as int is self->_line_starts at (line - 1)
        var end as int is calling self._line_end_offset with line
        return calling _sourcemap_substring with self->_source, start, end

    ## Returns the span covering all of `line` (without its terminator).
    ##
    ## For `"abc\n"`, `line_span(1)` is `(1, 1)..(1, 4)`. The end column is one
    ## past the last text byte, which is the conventional caret position after
    ## the line.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `line`: 1-indexed line number.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A `Span` from `(line, 1)` to `(line, line_len + 1)`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Allocates a temporary string to measure the line, releases it, and
    ## returns a value type. Panics when `line` is out of range.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var span as Span is calling map.line_span with 2
    ## ```
    weave line_span with line as int into Span:
        var text as string is calling self.line_text with line
        var n as int is text length
        banish text
        return with start is (with line is line, col is 1), end is (with line is line, col is (n + 1))

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Span helpers
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Builds a `Span` from two byte offsets.
    ##
    ## Offsets are clamped to `[0, source_len]`; `end_offset < start_offset`
    ## panics because a half-open span cannot run backwards. `start == end` is
    ## valid and denotes an empty span (a cursor).
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `start_offset`: inclusive byte offset.
    ## - `end_offset`: exclusive byte offset.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A `Span` with both positions resolved.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(log lines), no allocation. Panics on a backwards span.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var span as Span is calling map.span_at with 0, 4
    ## ```
    weave span_at with start_offset as int, end_offset as int into Span:
        if end_offset < start_offset:
            calling spark.panic with "SourceMap.span_at: end before start"
        var start as Position is calling self.position_at with start_offset
        var end as Position is calling self.position_at with end_offset
        return with start is start, end is end

    ## Returns the two positions of `span` as a tuple.
    ##
    ## This is a convenience for callers that pattern-match on `(start, end)`
    ## instead of reading `span.start`/`span.end`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `span`: the span to unpack.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `(span.start, span.end)`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation.
    weave span_to_positions with span as Span into (Position, Position):
        return span.start, span.end

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Validation utilities
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## True when `offset` is in the valid half-open range `[0, source_len]`.
    ##
    ## The end offset is valid because it denotes "just past the last byte".
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation.
    weave is_valid_offset with offset as int into bool:
        return offset >= 0 and offset <= (calling self.source_len)

    ## True when `pos` addresses a real position of this source.
    ##
    ## Valid columns are `1..line_len + 1`; the extra column is the position
    ## just past the last byte of the line.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(line length), no allocation.
    weave is_valid_position with pos as Position into bool:
        if pos.line < 1 or pos.line > self->_line_starts.len:
            return false
        if pos.col < 1:
            return false
        var start as int is self->_line_starts at (pos.line - 1)
        var end as int is calling self._line_end_offset with pos.line
        return pos.col <= (end - start + 1)

    ## Clamps `offset` into `[0, source_len]`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no allocation.
    weave clamp_offset with offset as int into int:
        if offset < 0:
            return 0
        if offset > (calling self.source_len):
            return (calling self.source_len)
        return offset

    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Private helpers
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------

    ## Byte offset just past the text of `line`, excluding `\n` and a CRLF `\r`.
    ##
    ## ## Motivo
    ## `line_text`, `line_span` and `is_valid_position` must agree on what "the
    ## line" means; one private helper is the single source of truth.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1) reads; allocates nothing.
    weave _line_end_offset with line as int into int:
        var start as int is self->_line_starts at (line - 1)
        var end as int is (calling self.source_len)
        if line < self->_line_starts.len:
            set end is (self->_line_starts at line) - 1
        if end > start:
            var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of self->_source
            if ((raw at (end - 1)) to int) == SOURCEMAP_CARRIAGE_RETURN:
                set end is end - 1
        return end
